      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rather than doing a query and iterating through all the types every time we do an image capture, we should probably cache the information on startup.\n\nWe can keep a map of capture type to frame size (`std::array` would probably work since they\u0027re sequential and we know the max size; that would avoid using the heap with something like `std::unordered_map`)\n\nLet\u0027s also move the logic for constructing and interacting with that map into its own file so that we can keep things more abstracted and write unit tests for it. (e.g., don\u0027t expose the map directly, we can have a class that wraps it.)",
